  "details": "The container-tools module contains tools for working with containers, notably podman, buildah, skopeo, and runc.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * crun: crun: Arbitrary file creation/overwrite via symlink following (CVE-2026-47766)\n  * podman: podman: The `podman run` command can be instructed to disable almost all sandboxing - including user-requested sandboxing - by image annotation (CVE-2026-94603)\n  * net/textproto: mime/multipart: golang: golang: Denial of Service via memory limit bypass in multipart form parsing (CVE-2026-94440)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Bug in runc causes containers to fail to start with \"unsafe procfs detected: openat2 /proc/thread-self/fd/: function not implemented\" (JIRA:RHEL-133969)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
